        "alternatives",
        "evidence",
        "right-to-stop"
      ],
      "text": "I suggest acupuncture to the lower back: five fine single-use sterile needles, left for about twenty minutes while you lie face down. Guidelines differ: NICE in the UK advises against acupuncture for low back pain, while the American College of Physicians lists it among the first non-drug options. Risks are small — soreness, bruising, feeling faint, very rarely infection or injury to deeper structures. The alternatives are staying active, exercise or physiotherapy, and pain relief through your doctor. You can tell me to stop at any time."
    }
